-- One-time content update for the Zcash Free Society Hack program page.
-- Sets the public program page's ordered `content` sections (schedule, tracks,
-- themes, Privacy requirements, prizes, the Privacy rubric, the 30 days after,
-- FAQ) for slug 'free-society-hack-2026'.
-- Generated from client/src/lib/freeSocietyHackContent.ts. Keep the two in sync.
--
-- Safe before the program exists: the UPDATE matches no row until an admin
-- creates free-society-hack-2026. Re-run after creating it.
-- NOTE: this overwrites the program's current content for this row.

UPDATE programs
SET content = '[{"type":"schedule","title":"Schedule (IST)","rows":[{"time":"Wed 4 Nov 10:00","label":"Hack starts"},{"time":"Wed 4 Nov 20:00","label":"Evening judging (projects in by now)"},{"time":"Thu 5 Nov 00:00","label":"Submissions close"},{"time":"Thu 5 Nov 08:00","label":"Morning judging"},{"time":"Thu 5 Nov 10:30","label":"Demo line-up out"},{"time":"Thu 5 Nov 11:00","label":"Demo day"},{"time":"Thu 5 Nov 13:00","label":"Prize announcements"}]},{"type":"markdown","title":"Two tracks","body":"**Privacy (Zcash).** Build something people can use privately with shielded ZEC on testnet. Judged by five judges in Stadium.\n\n**Agentic Commerce (by Bitrefill).** An AI agent that searches, buys and pays on Bitrefill by itself. Judged and paid by Bitrefill.\n\nYou can enter one track or both. A project can win in both."},{"type":"markdown","title":"Themes (Privacy track)","body":"- **1.** Private payment rails\n- **2.** The first five minutes\n- **3.** Privacy beyond the transaction"},{"type":"markdown","title":"What a Privacy submission needs","body":"▢ **Works on testnet with NU7**, using shielded Orchard funds via unified addresses.\n\n▢ **A one-line pitch:** what it does and for whom.\n\n▢ **One testnet transaction id** your project created. Stadium checks that it exists and is shielded; amounts and memos stay private.\n\n▢ **A public URL** if it is an app people use.\n\n▢ **A demo video, 2 minutes max.** For non-apps it must show it working with Zcash.\n\n▢ **A public repo with a README.**\n\n▢ **Every technology you used.**\n\n▢ **A next milestone for the 30 days**, with links to anything already started.\n\nFriction notes are optional and not scored, but they go straight to the teams who can fix them.\n\n**Out of scope:** Zcash Shielded Assets, mainnet funds, Sprout, v4 transactions, zcashd wallet RPC."},{"type":"markdown","title":"Prizes","body":"**Privacy (USD, cash): five podium projects**\n\n- Top prize: $1,300 (one project)\n- Second prize: $300 (two projects)\n- Third prize: $200 (two projects)\n\n**Ecosystem Prize.** The judges pick two of the five podium projects, at any prize level. Each gets a partner and a 30-day milestone. Complete it and $100 more is released on Fri 11 Dec. If it is not completed, you keep your day prize.\n\n**Agentic Commerce (by Bitrefill)**\n\n- $1,000 · $800 · $600\n- $100 for the best feedback\n\nEach project names one point person; prizes go to that person."},{"type":"markdown","title":"How Privacy projects are judged","body":"Five criteria scored 0 to 3, plus a Bonus of 0 or 1. No weights.\n\n| Criterion | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Works: how much of the demonstrated core flow is real? | Nothing meaningfully interacts with Zcash | The Zcash interaction is mocked or simulated | Real shielded testnet interaction, but a core step is incomplete, manual or unverified | The demonstrated core flow works as intended, with no core step faked, manual or bypassed, and with verifiable evidence |\n| Private: does it protect information appropriately? | No meaningful privacy protection, or serious undisclosed exposure | Shielded transactions, but significant metadata or data exposure is not adequately addressed | Shielded transactions and a considered privacy design, with remaining limitations identified | Privacy is designed into the flow; disclosures are minimized, and remaining exposures and trust assumptions are clearly explained |\n| Easy: can its intended user use it? | Only the builder can use it | Usable with the builder''s help | Usable by the intended audience with the README or provided instructions | A representative user can complete the core task unaided, in minutes |\n| Needed: is there evidence of a real need? | No clear user or problem | A user is named, but the need is assumed | A specific user problem is explained and backed by evidence, such as a documented ecosystem gap or conversations with users | Strong validation: target users have requested it, a partner wants to adopt or pilot it, or users have demonstrated demand |\n| Continuing: is the builder moving it forward? | No next milestone | A vague plan | A concrete 30-day plan with an identifiable beneficiary | Already taking concrete steps: an upstream PR, an active issue, a partner discussion, a pilot or engaged users |\n| Bonus (0 or 1) | Nothing exceptional | Genuinely exceptional and not captured above: original technical contribution, elegant solution, or reusable ecosystem contribution | | |\n\nMaximum 16. A project whose average Works score is 0 can''t win. Ties go to the higher Continuing score, then the higher Needed score. Agentic Commerce uses Bitrefill''s criteria."},{"type":"markdown","title":"The 30 days after","body":"Every builder gets two short check-ins by email: **Thu 19 Nov** and **Fri 4 Dec**. Two questions: still building, and one link to what you did since the hack.\n\nThe two Ecosystem Prize projects also track their milestone here:\n\n1. Agree the milestone with your partner by **Fri 13 Nov**\n2. Check in **Thu 19 Nov**\n3. Deliver it with a public link by **Fri 4 Dec** (partner confirms)\n4. Share it at a ZecHub Friday Lounge by **Fri 4 Dec**\n5. $100 released **Fri 11 Dec**"},{"type":"markdown","title":"FAQ","body":"**Who can submit?** Builders checked in at Capital Social, BKC, Mumbai. Use the email you registered with on Luma; that person is the project''s point person.\n\n**Can I enter both tracks?** Yes. Pick \"Both\" on the form and include a testnet transaction id.\n\n**Do I need real ZEC?** No. Testnet only. Mainnet funds are out of scope.\n\n**When do projects appear?** As soon as you submit, on this page.\n\n**Can I stay anonymous?** Yes. Tick \"I want to be anonymous\" on the form and your name and your teammates'' names are hidden on the public page. Organisers can still see them."}]'::jsonb,
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE slug = 'free-society-hack-2026';
